# Database Schema – MVP Fitness Coaching App

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This schema is optimized for:
> - **Invite-only, pay-gated access** (no public signup)
> - **Daily check-ins** as the core interaction
> - **Coach review queue** with red-flag detection
> - **WhatsApp-first** communication
> - **Privacy and compliance** (Singapore PDPA)
> - **Single-coach MVP** with multi-coach scalability
> - **No technical debt**

---

## Core Tables

### 1. **users**
*Authentication and basic profile for both coaches and clients*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `email` | String | ✓ | Unique, lowercase |
| `phone` | String | ✓ | Format: +65XXXXXXXX (Singapore) |
| `password_hash` | String | ✓ | Hashed with bcrypt/Argon2 |
| `role` | Enum | ✓ | `coach` \| `client` |
| `name` | String | ✓ | Full name |
| `avatar_url` | String | ✗ | Profile photo (S3/CDN) |
| `timezone` | String | ✓ | Default: `Asia/Singapore` |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |
| `updated_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:** Single user table keeps auth simple. Role differentiation happens at application level.

**Indexes:**
- `email` (unique)
- `phone` (unique)
- `role` (for filtering)

---

### 2. **coaches**
*Extended profile for coach users*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `user_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `users.id` |
| `business_name` | String | ✗ | E.g., "Peak Performance SG" |
| `whatsapp_number` | String | ✓ | For client communication |
| `stripe_account_id` | String | ✗ | For future billing integration |
| `onboarding_complete` | Boolean | ✓ | Default: false |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:** Keeps coach-specific data separate. Extensible for multi-coach businesses later.

**Constraints:**
- One coach per user (`user_id` unique)

---

### 3. **clients**
*Extended profile for client users + coach assignment*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `user_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `users.id` |
| `coach_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `coaches.id` |
| `status` | Enum | ✓ | `active` \| `paused` \| `inactive` |
| `start_date` | Date | ✓ | Program start date |
| `target_weight_kg` | Decimal | ✗ | Optional goal |
| `target_waist_cm` | Decimal | ✗ | Optional goal |
| `daily_step_goal` | Integer | ✗ | E.g., 10000 |
| `birthday` | Date | ✗ | For age calculation |
| `consent_whatsapp` | Boolean | ✓ | PDPA compliance |
| `consent_data_processing` | Boolean | ✓ | PDPA compliance |
| `onboarding_complete` | Boolean | ✓ | Default: false |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |
| `updated_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:** 
- Coach relationship is explicit and portable (client can switch coaches)
- Status enables pausing without data loss
- Consent fields are mandatory for Singapore PDPA

**Indexes:**
- `coach_id, status` (for coach dashboard filtering)
- `user_id` (unique)

---

## Daily Check-Ins

### 4. **check_ins**
*The heartbeat of the app – daily client submissions*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `client_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `clients.id` |
| `date` | Date | ✓ | Check-in date (client's timezone) |
| `steps` | Integer | ✓ | Daily step count |
| `hunger_level` | Integer | ✓ | Scale 1-10 |
| `energy_level` | Integer | ✓ | Scale 1-10 |
| `weight_kg` | Decimal | ✗ | Optional daily weigh-in |
| `waist_cm` | Decimal | ✗ | Optional measurement |
| `meal_photo_url` | String | ✗ | S3/CDN URL |
| `notes` | Text | ✗ | Client's free text |
| `submitted_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | Actual submission time |
| `reviewed_by_coach` | Boolean | ✓ | Default: false |
| `reviewed_at` | Timestamp | ✗ | When coach reviewed |
| `coach_notes` | Text | ✗ | Private coach notes |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- `date` vs `submitted_at`: Date is for grouping, timestamp for late submissions
- `reviewed_by_coach`: Powers the coach review queue
- Optional fields allow quick 30-second logging

**Indexes:**
- `client_id, date` (unique – one check-in per day)
- `client_id, reviewed_by_coach, date` (powers review queue)
- `date` (for time-series queries)

**Red Flag Logic** (application layer):
- `energy_level < 4` → Flag
- `hunger_level > 7` → Flag
- Missing check-in for 2+ days → Flag

---

## Progress Tracking

### 5. **progress_photos**
*Visual progress tracking separate from check-ins*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `client_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `clients.id` |
| `photo_url` | String | ✓ | S3/CDN URL (encrypted at rest) |
| `photo_type` | Enum | ✓ | `front` \| `side` \| `back` |
| `taken_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | When photo was taken |
| `weight_kg` | Decimal | ✗ | Weight at time of photo |
| `notes` | Text | ✗ | Client notes |
| `visibility` | Enum | ✓ | `coach_only` \| `client_visible` |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Separate from check-ins: photos are less frequent
- `visibility`: Client may want coach-only photos
- `photo_type`: Enables before/after comparisons

**Privacy:**
- Encrypt URLs or use signed S3 URLs
- PDPA requires explicit consent (tracked in `clients` table)

**Indexes:**
- `client_id, taken_at` (for chronological view)

---

### 6. **measurements**
*Weekly/biweekly structured measurements*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `client_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `clients.id` |
| `measured_at` | Date | ✓ | Measurement date |
| `weight_kg` | Decimal | ✗ | |
| `waist_cm` | Decimal | ✗ | |
| `hip_cm` | Decimal | ✗ | |
| `chest_cm` | Decimal | ✗ | |
| `body_fat_pct` | Decimal | ✗ | If using InBody etc. |
| `notes` | Text | ✗ | |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Structured measurements separate from daily check-ins
- Enables charting and progress comparison
- All measurements optional (flexibility)

**Indexes:**
- `client_id, measured_at` (for charts)

---

## Meal Plans

### 7. **meal_plans**
*Coach-created meal plan templates*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `coach_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `coaches.id` |
| `name` | String | ✓ | E.g., "Week 1 – High Protein" |
| `description` | Text | ✗ | Overview for coach |
| `pdf_url` | String | ✗ | S3/CDN link to PDF |
| `is_template` | Boolean | ✓ | Reusable template vs one-off |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |
| `updated_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Coaches can reuse templates across clients
- PDF-first for MVP (easier for coaches to create)
- `is_template`: Separates library from active assignments

---

### 8. **meal_plan_items**
*Individual meals/days within a plan (optional for MVP)*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `meal_plan_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `meal_plans.id` |
| `day_number` | Integer | ✓ | Day 1, 2, 3... |
| `meal_type` | Enum | ✓ | `breakfast` \| `lunch` \| `dinner` \| `snack` |
| `description` | Text | ✓ | E.g., "Grilled chicken + broccoli" |
| `calories` | Integer | ✗ | |
| `protein_g` | Integer | ✗ | |
| `carbs_g` | Integer | ✗ | |
| `fats_g` | Integer | ✗ | |

**Why:**
- Enables in-app meal plan viewing
- Optional for MVP if coaches prefer PDFs
- Can backfill later without schema changes

**Constraints:**
- `meal_plan_id, day_number, meal_type` (unique)

---

### 9. **client_meal_plans**
*Assignment of meal plans to clients*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `client_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `clients.id` |
| `meal_plan_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `meal_plans.id` |
| `start_date` | Date | ✓ | When plan begins |
| `end_date` | Date | ✗ | Optional expiry |
| `status` | Enum | ✓ | `active` \| `completed` \| `replaced` |
| `assigned_by_coach_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `coaches.id` |
| `assigned_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Tracks meal plan history (important for review)
- `status`: Allows replacing plans without deleting history
- Client can have multiple plans over time

**Indexes:**
- `client_id, status` (to fetch active plan)

---

## Sessions & Billing

### 10. **packages**
*Session packages purchased by clients*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `client_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `clients.id` |
| `total_sessions` | Integer | ✓ | E.g., 10 |
| `used_sessions` | Integer | ✓ | Default: 0 |
| `price_sgd` | Decimal | ✓ | In Singapore dollars |
| `purchased_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |
| `expires_at` | Date | ✗ | Optional expiry |
| `status` | Enum | ✓ | `active` \| `expired` \| `completed` |

**Why:**
- Simple package tracking for MVP
- `used_sessions`: Decremented on session log
- Stripe integration happens at purchase (not schema-level)

**Business Logic:**
- When `used_sessions >= total_sessions` → `status = completed`
- When `expires_at < now()` → `status = expired`

---

### 11. **sessions**
*Individual coaching session logs*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `client_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `clients.id` |
| `package_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `packages.id` |
| `coach_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `coaches.id` |
| `session_date` | Timestamp | ✓ | When session occurred |
| `duration_minutes` | Integer | ✗ | E.g., 60 |
| `notes` | Text | ✗ | Coach notes |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Tracks session usage against packages
- `notes`: Persistent session record
- Links to specific package for billing clarity

**Indexes:**
- `client_id, session_date` (for history view)
- `package_id` (to calculate `used_sessions`)

---

### 12. **payments**
*Payment records for compliance and history*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `client_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `clients.id` |
| `package_id` | UUID | ✗ | FK → `packages.id` (if applicable) |
| `amount_sgd` | Decimal | ✓ | Amount in SGD |
| `currency` | String | ✓ | Always `SGD` for MVP |
| `payment_method` | Enum | ✓ | `stripe` \| `paynow` \| `cash` \| `bank_transfer` |
| `stripe_payment_intent_id` | String | ✗ | Stripe reference |
| `status` | Enum | ✓ | `pending` \| `completed` \| `failed` \| `refunded` |
| `paid_at` | Timestamp | ✗ | When payment confirmed |
| `notes` | Text | ✗ | E.g., "PayNow ref: 123456" |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Supports multiple payment methods (Stripe + local SG methods)
- `stripe_payment_intent_id`: Links to Stripe webhooks
- `notes`: Captures offline payment details

**Compliance:**
- Required for PDPA (financial records retention)
- Audit trail for disputes

---

## Messaging & Automation

### 13. **messages**
*In-app messages between coach and client*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `client_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `clients.id` |
| `sender_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `users.id` |
| `content` | Text | ✓ | Message body |
| `message_type` | Enum | ✓ | `manual` \| `automated` |
| `sent_via` | Enum | ✓ | `in_app` \| `whatsapp` |
| `whatsapp_message_id` | String | ✗ | For WhatsApp API tracking |
| `read_at` | Timestamp | ✗ | When recipient read it |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Unified message log for in-app + WhatsApp
- `message_type`: Differentiates automation from human
- `sent_via`: Tracks channel for analytics

**Privacy:**
- Messages older than 90 days can be archived (PDPA)

**Indexes:**
- `client_id, created_at` (for conversation view)

---

### 14. **automated_message_rules**
*Automation triggers for coach efficiency*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `coach_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `coaches.id` |
| `trigger_type` | Enum | ✓ | `daily_reminder` \| `missed_checkin` \| `low_energy` \| `high_hunger` |
| `message_template` | Text | ✓ | E.g., "Hey {name}, don't forget your check-in!" |
| `send_via` | Enum | ✓ | `whatsapp` \| `in_app` \| `both` |
| `is_active` | Boolean | ✓ | Default: true |
| `trigger_time` | Time | ✗ | E.g., "20:00" for daily reminder |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |
| `updated_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Coaches can customize automation per their style
- `{name}`, `{coach_name}` placeholders for personalization
- `is_active`: Turn off without deleting

**Example Triggers:**
- `daily_reminder` at 8 PM if no check-in today
- `missed_checkin` after 2 days of no check-ins
- `low_energy` when `energy_level < 4` for 3+ days

---

### 15. **notifications**
*Push notifications and in-app alerts*

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|-------|------|----------|-------|
| `id` | UUID | ✓ | Primary key |
| `user_id` | UUID | ✓ | FK → `users.id` |
| `title` | String | ✓ | Notification title |
| `body` | Text | ✓ | Notification body |
| `notification_type` | Enum | ✓ | `check_in_reminder` \| `red_flag` \| `new_message` \| `new_meal_plan` |
| `reference_id` | UUID | ✗ | E.g., `check_in.id` or `message.id` |
| `read_at` | Timestamp | ✗ | |
| `created_at` | Timestamp | ✓ | |

**Why:**
- Separate from messages for in-app notifications
- `reference_id`: Deep linking to relevant screen
- Powers coach "unread alerts" count

**Indexes:**
- `user_id, read_at` (for unread count)

